=== layout: one-panel

# *Gene Mapping*

@body

![Slide image 1](assets/lect08d-3_point_testcross_voss/image_001.svg)

- A heterozygote fruit fly for all three genes, was crossed with a homozygous recessive for all three genes, making the following results a [valid test-cross]{color=red}.
- Progeny are sorted by phenotype name.

=== layout: one-panel

# *Steps in Three-Point Test-Cross Gene Map*

@body

- 1. Determine parental genotype
- 2\: Pick any two genes
  - completely cover up the third so it does not confuse you!!!
- 3. Determine which of the progeny are parental and non-parental genotypes
- 4. Determine the map distance between the two genes
  - 4a Sum the progeny from the non-parental genotypes
  - 4b. Divide the NP by the total progeny
  - 4c. Multiply the result by 100% to get the distance between the genes
- 5. Go to Step 2 and pick a new pair of genes until all pairs are complete
- 6. Use all the gene distances to determine the order of the genes.
  - largest distance are furthest away and on the ends

